==English==
{{wp}}
{{wikidata lexeme|L19999}}
[[File:Alignment (PSF).png|thumb|In alignment and out of alignment]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|aline}} {{qual|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|alynen}}, {{m|enm|alinen||copulate}}, from {{der|en|frm|aligner}}, from {{der|en|fro|alignier}}, from {{m|fro|a-}} + {{m|fro|lignier}}, from {{der|en|la|lineo|lineare|make straight or perpendicular}}, from the noun {{m|la|linea||line}}, from {{m|la|līneus||[[flaxen]]; flaxen [thing]}}, from {{m|la|līnum||[[flax]]}}, likely ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*līnom}} (compare {{m|en|linen}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/əˈlaɪn/|/æˈlaɪn/|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-align.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/əˈlaɪn/|a=GA}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪn|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[form]] a [[line]]; to fall into line.
#: {{ux|en|The pedestrians '''aligned''' in such a way that from above they made a pyramidal pattern.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[adjust]] to a line; to [[range]] or form in line; to bring into line.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[organize]] in a [[consistent]], [[defined]] way, perhaps in an [[abstract]] [[sense]].
# {{lb|en|intransitive|reflexive}} To [[identify]] (oneself) with, match, or support the behaviour, thoughts, etc. of another person, organization, or country.
#: {{syn|en|ally|support|side with}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|computing}} To [[store]] ([[data]]) in a way that is [[consistent]] with the [[memory]] [[architecture]], i.e. by beginning each item at an [[offset]] equal to some multiple of the [[word]] [[size]].
# {{lb|en|transitive|bioinformatics}} To organize a [[linear]] [[arrangement]] of [[DNA]], [[RNA]]{{,}} or [[protein]] [[sequence]]s which have regions of similarity.
# {{lb|en|transitive|information science}} To identify [[entity|entities]] that refer to the same [[real-world]] [[object]] in different [[knowledge base]]s.

